alex: Hey — trying to get the JS SDK to work in Deno and Bun edge runtimes. Hitting two things: import resolution (import maps + conditional exports) and auth retries seem broken in edge because timers/stack traces differ. Anyone seen this?

marta: ugh yes. what error do you see for imports?

alex: In Deno: 

Error: Cannot resolve module 'redwood'

I use import_map.json to alias @redwood/sdk -> ./dist/mod.mjs but Deno still resolves to the package root because of package.json exports?

sam: Deno ignores package.json exports unless you use a URL import or a file path. If you publish only an "exports" field that points to conditional entries, Deno may not map bare specifiers the same as Node. Import map should map the bare specifier to a file URL or relative path. Example import_map.json: 

{
  "imports": {
    "@redwood/sdk": "./dist/mod.mjs"
  }
}

Then run: `deno run --allow-net --import-map=import_map.json mod.ts`

ben: Also check that your published package has the mjs file at dist/mod.mjs. Some bundlers output .cjs only. Deno needs ESM.

alex: Got that. Another wrinkle: Bun and CF Workers complain about `globalThis.crypto.subtle` missing or different shape. We rely on webcrypto to sign tokens for auth retry backoff. Error in Bun: `TypeError: globalThis.crypto.subtle is undefined`

marta: For edge runtimes, you can't assume node/web parity. Two approaches: ship a tiny runtime shim that polyfills subtle or use a pure-JS fallback (eg tweetnacl for HMAC). We tried to keep dependencies minimal, so we added a small conditional shim: 

// runtime-crypto.ts
export const subtle = (globalThis as any).crypto?.subtle ?? {
  digest: async (alg, data) => { /* fallback using libs */ }
};

Then in auth code: `const digest = await subtle.digest('SHA-256', buf)`

sam: Another thing I ran into: setTimeout behaves differently in some edge runtimes (Workers vs Bun). Our retry backoff used setTimeout + AbortController; in Cloudflare Workers setTimeout is available but doesn't return a Node Timer object — you only need to pass a number into clearTimeout. In Bun it's similar but there are small scheduling differences that made tests flaky. We moved retry scheduling to a Promise-based sleep: `await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms))` which is safer.

alex: Good call. Any thoughts about typings? When publishing dual ESM/CJS we got duplicate declaration issues. Consumers in TS complain that `index.d.ts` is missing types for the ESM entrypoint.

ben: Make sure package.json has `types` pointing at the bundled d.ts (e.g., "types": "dist/index.d.ts") and that your exports include `"./package.json": { "default": "./package.json" }`? Also include separate export entries for types: 

"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/mod.mjs",
    "require": "./dist/mod.cjs",
    "types": "./dist/index.d.ts"
  }
}

TS will pick up the types if the package root types field points correctly.

marta: For Deno users, also publish a small `mod.ts` that re-exports the ESM entry so they can import via URL: `https://cdn.example.com/redwood/mod.ts` — that avoids import maps for many users.

alex: Nice. One more weird bug: auth token automatic refresh was not happening in edge because we rely on a background timer to refresh 60s before expiry, but Workers can cold-start and the timer gets lost. Should rely on lazy refresh on first request plus a short in-flight singleflight to avoid stampeding.

sam: Agreed. Implemented pattern: on request, check expiry. If < threshold triggerRefresh() but await singleflight promise so concurrent callers wait on one refresh. If refresh fails, fallback to existing token if still valid for short window, else return 401.

alex: Thanks. I'm going to: 1) publish an explicit mod.mjs for Deno and add import_map advice in docs, 2) add small crypto fallback, 3) switch retries to Promise sleep, 4) update types/exports and add mod.ts for CDN.

devex-bot: Reminder: please file a tiny RFC in /docs/devex with the change list and add a sample Deno quickstart in examples/deno-quickstart. I'll create a checklist PR template. :thumbsup:

ben: If anyone wants I can draft the mod.ts and import_map snippet and a one-file Bun example demonstrating fetch auth + retry behavior.

marta: clap :) That would help new users a lot.

alex: Great — assign to me and ben, I'll open PRs in the SDK repo today.

sam: ping me for review, I'll run it against our internal edge smoke tests.

alex: thanks all :rocket:
